# Line endings are part of the build material (T081-C01).
#
# Found by the T081 clean-room run: this repo ships tests that assert on file
# *content* (`tests/contracts/guard.test.ts` reads `.gitignore`,
# `tests/unit/doctor.test.ts` reads the `docs/operations/*.md` command blocks).
# Committed blobs are LF, but with `core.autocrlf=true` — the default on many
# Windows installs — `git archive`/checkout rewrites them to CRLF, so those
# assertions passed in the author's working tree and failed in a fresh
# extraction of the same commit. Pinning the eol makes the checked-out bytes
# identical to the committed bytes on every machine.
#
# `text=auto` keeps git's binary detection, so `feini-brain-mvp-spec-v2.zip`
# and other binaries are untouched.
#
# If a Windows batch/PowerShell entry point is ever added, it needs its own
# `eol=crlf` rule; none is tracked today.
* text=auto eol=lf
